# Research lanes — offload big reads

Before a large-context read yourself (long doc, unfamiliar repo, multi-file
"where/why", verifying a claim across a codebase), hand it to a research lane and
read back only the cited answer. General rule, not project-scoped. Wrappers on
PATH, uniform interface:
`<wrapper> [-C dir] [-e low|medium|high] [-m model] [-v] "<question>"`

**Pick provider + model + effort dynamically, by task fit — never one default:**

- `gemini-think` — biggest context, fastest, cheapest, multimodal. For: digest
  huge docs / log dumps / whole-repo sweeps, high-volume lookups, screenshots.
- `cursor-think` — built-in codebase retrieval, frontier models, `--mode ask`
  read-only. For: "where is X in this code", code-aware Q&A, plan a change.
- `codex-think` — strongest deliberate reasoning, tunable effort, but
  rate-limited + re-reads repo AGENTS.md each call. For: subtle root-cause,
  architecture tradeoff, security reasoning. Also `-e ultra`.
- `geminiweb-think` — Gemini web app on a paid plan (cookie auth), a **separate
  quota pool** from `gemini-think`'s API key. For: when `gemini-think` is
  drained, or a top-model / `--deep` Deep Research answer. No repo traversal.
  (Optional/unofficial — omit this line if you didn't set it up.)
- Answer really matters → run two lanes on different providers, cross-check
  (`lane-compare "<q>"`).

`-e` steps effort: `low` = lookup/verify, none/`medium` = normal research,
`high` = hard multi-step. Each wrapper maps `-e` to a concrete backend model;
`-m` overrides.

**Before delegating, run `lane-budget`** (local ledger — no backend has a usage
API). GREEN = use freely; YELLOW = only if this lane is the genuine best fit;
RED / cooldown = only if nothing else can do the task. Every `*-think` wrapper
calls `lane-guard` first and **refuses** a RED lane (override: `LANE_FORCE=1
<wrapper> …`, sparingly). `lane-cool <lane> <minutes>` parks a lane RED manually
when you know a backend is spent.

Read-only by convention — the primary agent does all writes. On a quota/tier
error: stop retrying that lane, switch or wait.
